module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.generic_alias_callable_not_instantiated

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data generic_alias_callable_not_instantiated: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "generic_alias_callable_not_instantiated" as NonEmptyStr,
  receipts: [
    "**a callable whose function type is reached through a GENERIC type alias is not instantiated back to its arrow, so nothing downstream recognises it as callable** (a value declared `ApplicationUnary<Int>`, where `type ApplicationUnary<T> = fn(T) -> T`, refuses at its call site with `function '<name>' not found in scope`, while the identical value declared `fn(Int) -> Int` or through a NON-generic alias resolves. Alias peeling already works; instantiation of the type ARGUMENT is what is missing. " ,
    "MEASURED 2026-09-08 while repairing gunbc#10625, eleven cells in one module, each compiling its subject as a source string so the module itself resolves and every assertion returns a real verdict rather than an infrastructure fact. Enrolled at function grain in gunbc.explicit_witness_admission; the executing witnesses are v1.tests.claim.algebra_receiver_callable_witness_test. " ,
    "THE THREE CELLS THAT LOCATE IT hold the field, the shorthand match binder, the position and the call fixed and vary ONLY how the function type is spelled: `g: fn(Int) -> Int` PASSES, `h: IntFn` where `type IntFn = fn(Int) -> Int` PASSES, `step: ApplicationUnary<Int>` FAILS. The generic instantiation is the whole variable. " ,
    "FOUR EARLIER CAUSES WERE REPORTED AS ESTABLISHED AND ALL FOUR ARE REFUTED BY CELLS IN THE SAME FILE, which is the part worth carrying: binder SPELLING (shorthand and explicit both refuse), NAME COLLISION (a pool-free name refuses), BINDER KIND (a match binder resolves over a literal arrow), and POSITION (same arm, same nesting, resolves). A fifth, that bare-call resolution omits the lexical scope because v1.compiler.infer_lookup.global_bare_callable_node takes only (type_env, name), is a true fact about that function and does not decide these cells -- a literal-arrow call traverses the same path and resolves. " ,
    "THE MECHANISM THAT PRODUCED FOUR WRONG CAUSES IS THE REUSABLE LESSON: the generic alias was the declared type in EVERY refusing cell and absent from EVERY passing one, so it partitioned the table exactly as well as each story being told, and no cell could separate them. A probe table proves a partition, not a cause; any variable perfectly correlated with the partition is equally consistent with it. Before naming a cause, enumerate what is CONSTANT across the reds and ABSENT from the greens, and author a cell varying one of those against a control holding the rest fixed. " ,
    "A NARROW CLOSURE MANUFACTURED STRUCTURE THAT IS NOT IN THE LANGUAGE. Run under `claim_batch --entry` with four modules in closure, two cells RESOLVED whose only distinction was that the binder was spelled `step`, a name one other corpus declaration carries; the required floor at 2629 modules refuses all four uniformly. Three hypotheses were built on that artifact. For a question about NAME RESOLUTION the floor is the oracle and a narrow run is a hypothesis generator only. " ,
    "WHY NOTHING EVER REDDENED, and it is a property of the corpus rather than an absence of evidence: v2.lens.testgen CorpusLensDriver is the ONLY generic function-type alias in the tree, and the name occurs exactly once -- its own declaration. Nothing is declared with it and nothing calls it, so the single construct that could exercise this class is itself dead. The WORKING shape is live by contrast: six non-generic function-type aliases are declared. Nobody wrote the broken shape and everybody wrote the working one. " ,
    "CENSUS HAZARD FOR WHOEVER RE-DERIVES THESE COUNTS: this corpus embeds .dag and Rust source inside string literals, 4310 of 5234 .dag files carry at least one, and a regex over raw files reads fixture payloads and emitted Rust as corpus declarations -- that produced six false positives out of six in one census of this same question. Strip string literals first and anchor the match inside a parameter list at line start. A count of 115 fn-typed parameters bare-called in their own bodies is identical before and after stripping under that guard. " ,
    "A SECOND CLASS IS BLOCKED BEHIND THIS ONE, measured 2026-09-08 and recorded here because the blocked party has no other home. gunbc#10625 carries a heal-authored commit (2e4981d1af) removing the `local_call_refused` EARLY RETURN in infer_expr_body, and DESIGN 5 asks for an executed control that the removal cannot fabricate rather than an argument that it cannot. THE SEARCH, so it is not repeated: a body-local bound from a wrong-arity generic alias (`type Fn1<T> = fn(T) -> T`, `type BadFn = Fn1<Int, Int>`) and then called refuses at head with 4 blocking errors; zeroing the `local_call_diags` concat in the mirror, rebuilding and re-running gives 2 and STILL refuses, because the alias-arity errors are raised independently at the DECLARATION site. So on that shape the local-call channel is not load-bearing for the stop, and neither was the early return -- but the shape does not ISOLATE the channel, so it is not the control. The clean positive control the isolating probe needs is a let-bound callable typed through a generic alias, called by name, and that construct is broken by THIS class: it refuses with `function 'f' not found in scope` at correct arity, reproduced through the emitter rather than a census. Written as NOT FOUND WITH THE SEARCH SHOWN, never as cannot exist -- DESIGN 5 names 'never' as the trap that lets a ratchet pass for a wall, and no shape has been shown impossible here. " ,
    "SO THE MISSING HARNESS IS THIS CLASS ITSELF, which DESIGN 4b addresses directly: where no fixture harness can express the subject, that missing harness is the next-rung trigger rather than a permanent ceiling. The isolating control for the removed fail-closed arm becomes WRITABLE, and is owed, at the moment the capability in the next-rung trigger below lands -- a callable typed through a generic alias resolves. One capability retires two obligations, which is why they are rostered together rather than filed apart. " ,
    "RUNG: outside the modeled guarantee at the source-to-interpretation boundary, held by enrolled discriminating REDs with accepted positive controls beside them (the literal-arrow and non-generic-alias cells, which pass). The class is real and decidable and has no live corpus site, which is exactly the situation where the enrolled RED is the entire protection: nothing else in the tree would go red on it. " ,
    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, as a capability: a GENERIC function-type alias is instantiated to its arrow wherever a callable is recognised, so a value declared `ApplicationUnary<Int>` is callable exactly as one declared `IntFn` or `fn(Int) -> Int` already is. The trigger names INSTANTIATION and not alias peeling deliberately -- peeling already works, so a trigger naming it would be satisfied by machinery that changes nothing while the capability stayed dead. Greening is the counted un-quarantine event: the six admission rows delete in the same change that lands the fix, and the unchanged witnesses become permanent regression controls.)" ,
  ],
  evidence: [],
}
